ype":"Button"},{"config":{"icon":"camera","label":{"$i18n":"evidence.captureN"},"value":3,"variant":"primary","visible":false},"id":"capture-3","type":"Button"},{"config":{"icon":"camera","label":{"$i18n":"evidence.captureN"},"value":4,"variant":"primary","visible":false},"id":"capture-4","type":"Button"},{"config":{"icon":"camera","label":{"$i18n":"evidence.captureN"},"value":5,"variant":"primary","visible":false},"id":"capture-5","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Panel"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Readiness: Capture slide-over","spec":{"accessibility":["A row's state is said by its icon and, for assistive technology, in words (not captured, queued, capturing, captured, failed); every row is a checkbox named by its context.","The progress is also stated as text, \"N of M done\"."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Panel, Stack, Text, Select, SelectOption, Checkbox, Button, Icon, Image); the progress bar is two Stacks, the highlight of an added row is a separate row, and the thumbnails are a sample Asset in place of a screenshot.","The contexts of the rows are baked samples under readiness.sample.*; the Select values, the Variant names and the server sentence of a failed row are sample content.","The four selects have no leading icons, the progress bar has no progressbar role and the screen-reader announcements are not modelled; the English sentence of the server and the catalog line under it are both shown in every Locale, where the Workbench shows the catalog line only once in en-US.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities and the server sentence; en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A holder of evidence.capture on a desktop layout pressed Capture… in the Evidence facet, Capture again in the Evidence viewer, or Capture these again for the stale captures; the slide-over opens at the right edge.","The base state lists one context, the one the canvas shows now: Base state, desktop 1920 × 1080, en-US, light, ticked.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the slide-over is never wider than the viewport."],"intent":"Show the Capture Evidence slide-over of the Readiness panel as built from Adapter Widgets only: an explicit list of resolved render contexts of the View, the convenience buttons that grow that list, and the progress, results and failures of capturing the checked rows one at a time.","interactionRules":["Only the contexts listed are captured and nothing expands on its own: Add to list adds the context chosen in the four selects, and the All Variants, All locales, All viewports and All themes buttons first grow the visible list from the ticked rows; nothing runs until Capture.","Capture runs exactly the ticked rows that are not captured yet, one context at a time, each from a fresh Runtime; a row shows queued, capturing, captured with a thumbnail or failed with the reason, and one failure never hides the others.","While capturing, the controls that change the list are disabled and the slide-over cannot be dismissed; Stop after this one leaves the remaining rows not captured, and the progress shows how many contexts are done of the total.","A failed row says why under the server's own sentence in the Workbench language, for example a failed kit build, a bound Asset that did not load or an invalid Adapter set, and can be removed or captured again."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"opened-from","type":"view","viewId":"e9f5d101-3a1b-4c2d-9e4f-6b7c8d9eaf01"}],"requirements":["01a115cd-c3c9-76fd-8ccd-4a8664e52e7d","01a115cd-c3fd-7e82-aa05-737aac6c4354","01a115cd-c395-72b0-be67-4a77c4d2ade4"]},